## 2. Definitions

"Licensor" means Ziyang Tan, operating the bBpiano project under the name
bBSonicLab, or a successor rights holder authorized to license the Licensed
Software.

"You" means the individual or legal entity exercising rights under this
license.

"Official Distribution" means the unmodified Licensed Software obtained
from a source expressly designated by the Licensor.

"Documentation" means user-facing documentation officially published by
the Licensor describing supported command-line and other public interfaces.

"Extension" means independently developed software that interacts with an
Official Distribution through interfaces described in the Documentation or
ordinary operating-system process interfaces, without incorporating any
portion of the Licensed Software. An Extension may be a script, plug-in,
application, or other independently authored component.

"Commercial Extension or Integration" means an Extension or integration
that is sold, licensed for a fee, monetized, supplied as part of a paid
product or service, or otherwise offered to third parties in a commercial
context. Internal scripts used solely to automate otherwise permitted use
of the Licensed Software, without being offered as a product or service to
third parties, are not Commercial Extensions solely because the user operates
a business or earns income from the resulting work.

"Hosted Service" means a network-accessible service, API, shared synthesis
service, or comparable offering through which third parties access or obtain
the Licensed Software's synthesis functionality, whether for payment or free
of charge. Ordinary internal use across devices controlled by You, without
providing that functionality to third parties, is not a Hosted Service.

"Protected Implementation Information" means non-public implementation-
specific information embodied in the Licensed Software, including source or
intermediate code, internal algorithms and architecture, DSP and physical-
modeling implementations, coefficients, presets, model parameters, calibration
data, internal structures, and implementation techniques. This definition
does not make independently known scientific principles, published facts,
or lawfully observable performance measurements proprietary merely by
naming them.

"Output" means audio, recordings, or other independently usable content
produced by an authorized operation of the Licensed Software. Output does
not include the Licensed Software itself, an Extension, extracted runtime
data, or Protected Implementation Information.

"Written Authorization" means a separate express permission from the
Licensor in writing, including an electronic written agreement or written
correspondence verifiably issued by the Licensor. An authorization may set
additional conditions for the activity it permits.

