## 4. Independent Extensions

You may create, use, and distribute non-commercial Extensions without
obtaining separate permission if each Extension:

1. communicates with the Licensed Software only through supported public
   interfaces described in the Documentation or ordinary operating-system
   process interfaces;
2. does not incorporate, modify, bundle, disclose, or redistribute the
   Licensed Software or Protected Implementation Information;
3. requires its users to obtain any required bBpiano copy separately from
   an Official Distribution; and
4. complies with Section 9 (Attribution).

A Commercial Extension or Integration requires the Licensor's prior Written
Authorization, even if it does not bundle or redistribute the Licensed
Software. An independently distributed non-commercial Extension does not
become commercial merely because an end user employs it while making a
recording or other Output for commercial use.

No provision in this section permits redistribution of the Licensed Software
itself. Bundling an Official Distribution with another product, installer,
package, or service requires separate prior Written Authorization.

